@page "/docs/extensions/captcha"

<Seo Canonical="/docs/extensions/captcha" Title="Blazorise Captcha component" Description="Learn how to use the Blazorise Captcha component to protect forms with provider-based captchas like reCAPTCHA." />

<DocsPageTitle Path="Extensions/Captcha" AddedVersion="1.5" AddedDate="2024-02-12">
    Blazorise Captcha component
</DocsPageTitle>

<DocsPageLead>
    Integrate simple captchas into your Blazor applications with the Blazorise Captcha component.
</DocsPageLead>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    This extension supports multiple captcha providers, enabling the addition of captcha functionality with provider-specific settings.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    To use the <Code>Captcha</Code> component, install the base package and a provider package first.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Supported captcha providers
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    <UnorderedList>
        <UnorderedListItem>
            <Strong>Google reCAPTCHA</Strong> implemented via <Strong>Blazorise.Captcha.ReCaptcha</Strong>.
        </UnorderedListItem>
    </UnorderedList>
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Installation
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Base package">
        Install the base captcha extension from NuGet.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionSource Code="CaptchaNugetInstallExample" />
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Provider package">
        Install the reCAPTCHA provider extension from NuGet.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionSource Code="ReCaptchaNugetInstallExample" />
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Register services">
        Incorporate reCAPTCHA services by adding the following code to the relevant sections of <Strong>Program.cs</Strong>.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionSource Code="ReCaptchaRegisterServicesExample" />
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Imports">
        In your main <Strong>_Imports.razor</Strong>, ensure you include:
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionSource Code="CaptchaImportsExample" />
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="Static files (reCAPTCHA)">
        <Paragraph>
            Google <Strong>reCAPTCHA</Strong> docs recommend adding the script to the end of the <Code Tag>head</Code> tag with <Code>async</Code> and <Code>defer</Code> attributes.
        </Paragraph>
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionSourceGroup AriaLabel="Blazor project type">
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="ReCaptchaResourcesExample" CodeTitle="WebAssembly">
            Update <Code>wwwroot/index.html</Code>.
        </DocsPageSectionSource>
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="ReCaptchaResourcesExample" CodeTitle="Blazor Server">
            Update <Code>_Layout.cshtml</Code> or <Code>_Host.cshtml</Code>, depending on your project template.
        </DocsPageSectionSource>
        <DocsPageSectionSource Code="ReCaptchaResourcesExample" CodeTitle="Blazor Web App">
            Update <Code>Components/App.razor</Code> in the server project.
        </DocsPageSectionSource>
    </DocsPageSectionSourceGroup>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Examples
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageSection>
    <DocsPageSectionHeader Title="ReCaptcha Checkbox">
        The following example demonstrates how to use the <Code>ReCaptcha</Code> integration.
        You can use the <Code>ReCaptchaOptions</Code> to configure the widget according to your needs.
    </DocsPageSectionHeader>
    <DocsPageSectionContent Code="ReCaptchaExample" Outlined FullWidth>
        <ReCaptchaExample />
    </DocsPageSectionContent>
</DocsPageSection>

<DocsPageApi>
    <DocsPageApiItem Url="docs/extensions/captcha/api" Name="<Captcha />" />
</DocsPageApi>

<DocsPageSubsectionTitle Title="ReCaptchaOptions" />

<DocsAttributes>
    <DocsAttributesItem Name="SiteKey" Type="string">
        The client side api key for google reCAPTCHA.
    </DocsAttributesItem>
    <DocsAttributesItem Name="Size" Type="ReCaptchaSize" Default="ReCaptchaSize.Normal">
        The size of the widget.
    </DocsAttributesItem>
    <DocsAttributesItem Name="Theme" Type="ReCaptchaTheme" Default="ReCaptchaTheme.Light">
        The color theme of the widget.
    </DocsAttributesItem>
    <DocsAttributesItem Name="BadgePosition" Type="ReCaptchaBadgePosition" Default="ReCaptchaBadgePosition.BottomEnd">
        Reposition the reCAPTCHA badge. 'inline' lets you position it with CSS.
        This option is only available for invisible reCAPTCHA.
    </DocsAttributesItem>
    <DocsAttributesItem Name="LanguageCode" Type="string" Default="en">
        Refer to: https://developers.google.com/recaptcha/docs/language
        Defaults to: 'en' (English (US))
    </DocsAttributesItem>
</DocsAttributes>